    {
      "id": "vKEsyHFk/OjRLKb74#AOPSXwkc",
      "title": "The drawing that reads best is kept",
      "narrative": "A board is solved more than one way, and the answers are weighed as drawn: crossings, line length and how well it fits the reference pane, which is as wide as the shell gives a drawing and as tall as the tuned 1.4 page shape makes that width, not the shell's own pane (ADR 0043). A block of cards wraps a wide rank or folds tall ranks into columns only where that reads better. Nobody authors the reading, and every variant is laid out fresh.",
